    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Mullery O’Gara is pleased to present No. 3 Oakfield Place to the market, a handsome double-fronted red-brick period home situated on a quiet cul-de-sac in the heart of Portobello. The accommodation is unusually well laid out over a single level, creating a wonderfully practical and spacious home.\r\n\r\nBeautifully presented throughout, this charming and extended home combines the character and proportions of a period property with a bright, contemporary layout. The house enjoys an abundance of natural light, generous room proportions and impressive ceiling height, alongside a wealth of original features, cast-iron fireplaces and solid timber flooring. Rooflights throughout the house further enhance the wonderful sense of light and space.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation briefly comprises a welcoming entrance hall with ceiling arch and rooflight. To the front are two well-proportioned bedrooms, one currently arranged as a home office with bespoke cabinetry, study area, built-in wardrobes and original cast-iron fireplace. A third bedroom is situated to the rear and features solid wood flooring, cast-iron fireplace and rooflight.\r\n\r\nAt the heart of the house is a magnificent open-plan living, dining and kitchen space, providing a generous and sociable room for both everyday life and entertaining. The living area features an original cast-iron fireplace, built-in shelving and rooflight, while the dining area benefits from a further rooflight, storage and a convenient guest WC. The well-equipped kitchen provides excellent storage and workspace, with a door leading directly to the rear courtyard garden. The family bathroom completes the accommodation and includes a bath with electric shower, WC, wash hand basin, towel radiator and storage, with plumbing for a washing machine.\r\n\r\nTo the rear is a private, low-maintenance courtyard garden, enclosed by attractive granite walls and providing a lovely outdoor space in this central city location. On-street permit parking is available to the front.\r\n\r\nThe location of Oakfield Place is exceptional. Tucked away just off Lombard Street West and Clanbrassil Street, the property enjoys the best of Portobello living, with an outstanding selection of independent cafés, restaurants, bars and local shops all within easy walking distance. Favourite neighbourhood spots include Bibis, Gaillot et Gray, Scéal bakery, The Fumbally and Alma.\r\n\r\nThe property is also exceptionally well connected, with the Luas, numerous bus routes and Dublin Bikes stations all within easy reach. St. Stephen’s Green, Grafton Street and Iveagh Gardens are within walking distance, while a wide selection of primary and secondary schools, Montessori and childcare facilities and third-level institutions are also close by.\r\n\r\nNo. 3 Oakfield Place is a wonderful opportunity to acquire a turnkey period home with real character, excellent proportions and an enviable position in one of Dublin 8’s most sought-after neighbourhoods, just minutes from the city centre."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall \r\nSolid wood flooring, arch, access to attic and rooflight. \r\n\r\nLiving/Dining/Kitchen \r\nSolid wood floor throughout \r\nLiving\r\nCast iron fireplace, built in shelving and rooflight. \r\n\r\nDining \r\nRooflight, door to storage off. \r\n\r\nKitchen  \r\nRange of kitchen units, sink unit, plumbed for dishwasher, door to garden. \r\n\r\nGuest w.c, \r\nW.c whb and timber flooring.  \r\n\r\nBedroom 1 (Front) \r\nSolid wood flooring. \r\n\r\nBedroom 2 (Front) \r\nSolid wood flooring, bespoke cabinetry and study area, built in wardrobes and cast iron fireplace. \r\n\r\nBedroom 3 (Rear)\r\n Solid wood flooring, cast iron fireplace and rooflight. \r\n\r\nBathroom\r\nBath, electric shower, w.c, whb, towel radiator, storage, plumbed for washing machine with tiled floor and part tiled walls. \r\n\r\nOutside \r\nLow maintenance garden to the rear with granite walls and gravel. On street permit parking to the front."
      },
